/-!
# The permutation model of `M₂₃`, its order, and the surjection from its presented group

This file defines the permutation model `TauCeti.Sporadic.M23` of the Mathieu group `M₂₃`: the
subgroup of `Equiv.Perm (Fin 23)` generated by the two permutations `M23.a` and `M23.b` of the
ATLAS files `M23G1-p23B0.m1` and `M23G1-p23B0.m2`. The files list the images of the points
`1, …, 23`; the point `i` of a file is the point `i - 1` of `Fin 23`, and each generator is written
as the product of its disjoint cycles in Mathlib's cycle notation. In the files' numbering,

```text
a = (1,2)(3,4)(7,8)(9,10)(13,14)(15,16)(19,20)(21,22),
b = (1,16,11,3)(2,9,21,12)(4,5,8,23)(6,22,14,18)(13,20)(15,17).
```

So `a` is an involution with seven fixed points and `b` has order `4` with three fixed points; the
orders `2`, `4` and `23` of `a`, `b` and `a * b` are recorded as a check on the transcription.
Reading the files as preimages instead of images would replace `b` by `b⁻¹`, which sends `0` to
`2` rather than `15`.

It then shows that the ATLAS presentation `M23G1-P1` carried by `TauCeti.SporadicName.presentation`
holds in the model. That presentation is on the standard generators of `M₂₃` and its words are
read left to right, while Mathlib composes permutations right to left, `(σ * τ) i = σ (τ i)`.
Reversing a word and inverting its letters exchanges the two conventions, so the presentation
generators are sent to `a⁻¹ = a` and `b⁻¹`. All nine transcribed relators evaluate to `1` at this
assignment. The convention matters: at the assignment `(a, b)` the sixth relator `(ab ab⁻¹ ab²)⁴`
sends `0` to `16`, although the power relators `a²`, `b⁴` and `(ab)²³` hold at both assignments.
Since `b = (b⁻¹)⁻¹`, the permutations `a` and `b⁻¹` generate the model. Extending the assignment
therefore gives a homomorphism from `TauCeti.SporadicName.M23.Group` whose range is exactly the
model, hence a surjection onto it; in particular the presented group is nontrivial.

Finally it computes the order of the model, `10200960 = 2⁷ · 3² · 5 · 7 · 11 · 23`. Along the base
`0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5` the model has basic orbits of lengths `23`, `22`, `21`, `20`, `3` and `16`. The
first four are those of a `4`-transitive group, and those four transversal lists directly establish
`4`-transitivity (hence `3`-, `2`- and `1`-transitivity and primitivity) of `M23` on `Fin 23`. The
pointwise stabilizer of `0, 1, 2, 3` has order `48`, with orbits of lengths `3` (the points
`4, 10, 16`, which complete `0, 1, 2, 3` to a heptad of the Steiner system `S(4, 7, 23)`) and `16`
on the remaining points, on which the pointwise stabilizer of `0, 1, 2, 3, 4` acts regularly. For
each `i < 6` an explicit list of elements of the model fixes `0, …, i - 1` and sends `i` to each
point of its basic orbit. The two generators, and every product `s * r` of an element `s` of the
`j`-th list with an element `r` of the `i`-th list for `i ≤ j`, sift through these lists from the
`i`-th on, which by `Subgroup.natCard_eq_prod_length_of_siftCheck` pins the order to the product of
their lengths. The sifts are run by `decide` in the kernel on fifteen permutations given by tables
of images: the two ATLAS generators and thirteen further elements of the model, each checked to be
a word in the tables of the preceding levels. The same argument shows that `0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5` is a
base: only the identity of the model fixes these six points. Through the surjection, the presented
group has at least `10200960` elements whenever it is finite.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.M23`: the permutation model of `M₂₃` on `23` points.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.M23.presentationImage`: the images `a` and `b⁻¹` of the presentation
  generators.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.M23.lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one`: every transcribed relator of
  the presentation of `M₂₃` evaluates to `1` at these images.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.M23.closure_range_presentationImage`: the images generate the model.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.M23.presentationHom`: the homomorphism from the presented group.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.exists_surjective_M23`: the presented group maps onto the model.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.card_M23`: the model has `10200960` elements.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.M23.stabilizerChain_six_eq_bot`: the points `0, …, 5` form a base.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.M23.isMultiplyPretransitive_four`: the model acts `4`-transitively on its `23`
  points.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.le_natCard_group_M23`: the presented group, when finite, has at least
  `10200960` elements.

## References

* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, representation `M23G1-p23B0` and presentation `M23G1-P1`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/>; generator image files
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/M23/mtx/M23G1-p23B0.m1> and
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/M23/mtx/M23G1-p23B0.m2>.
* C. C. Sims, *Computational methods in the study of permutation groups*, in Computational
  Problems in Abstract Algebra, Pergamon, 1970, 169–183.
* Á. Seress, *Permutation Group Algorithms*, Cambridge Tracts in Mathematics 152, Cambridge
  University Press, 2003, §4.1–§4.2.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti.Sporadic

/-- The first generator of the permutation model of `M₂₃`, from the ATLAS file `M23G1-p23B0.m1`:
the involution `(1,2)(3,4)(7,8)(9,10)(13,14)(15,16)(19,20)(21,22)` of the file, shifted to the
points `0, …, 22`. -/
def M23.a : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) :=
  c[0, 1] * c[2, 3] * c[6, 7] * c[8, 9] * c[12, 13] * c[14, 15] * c[18, 19] * c[20, 21]

/-- The second generator of the permutation model of `M₂₃`, from the ATLAS file `M23G1-p23B0.m2`:
the permutation `(1,16,11,3)(2,9,21,12)(4,5,8,23)(6,22,14,18)(13,20)(15,17)` of order `4` of the
file, shifted to the points `0, …, 22`. -/
def M23.b : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) :=
  c[0, 15, 10, 2] * c[1, 8, 20, 11] * c[3, 4, 7, 22] * c[5, 21, 13, 17] * c[12, 19] * c[14, 16]

/-- The permutation model of the Mathieu group `M₂₃`: the subgroup of `Equiv.Perm (Fin 23)`
generated by the permutations `M23.a` and `M23.b` of the ATLAS files `M23G1-p23B0.m1` and
`M23G1-p23B0.m2`. -/
def M23 : Subgroup (Equiv.Perm (Fin 23)) := Subgroup.closure {M23.a, M23.b}

namespace M23

/-- Unfolding equation for `M23.a`, whose body is not exposed. -/
theorem a_def :
    a = c[0, 1] * c[2, 3] * c[6, 7] * c[8, 9] * c[12, 13] * c[14, 15] * c[18, 19] * c[20, 21] :=
  (rfl)

/-- Unfolding equation for `M23.b`, whose body is not exposed. -/
theorem b_def :
    b = c[0, 15, 10, 2] * c[1, 8, 20, 11] * c[3, 4, 7, 22] * c[5, 21, 13, 17] * c[12, 19] *
      c[14, 16] :=
  (rfl)

/-- The permutation model `M23` is the subgroup generated by the ATLAS generators. This is the
unfolding lemma for `TauCeti.Sporadic.M23`, whose body is not exposed. -/
theorem M23_def : M23 = Subgroup.closure {a, b} := (rfl)

/-- The first ATLAS generator `a` belongs to `M23`. -/
theorem a_mem : a ∈ M23 := Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp)

/-- The second ATLAS generator `b` belongs to `M23`. -/
theorem b_mem : b ∈ M23 := Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp)

/-! ### Generator orders -/

/- The equations between explicit permutations of `Fin 23` in this file are closed by
`decide +kernel`: the elaborator's `decide` exhausts its recursion depth while evaluating
`Cycle.formPerm`, while the kernel checks each of them directly. -/

/-- The generator `M23.a`, given by its table of images; it is an involution. -/
private def aTable : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![1, 0, 3, 2, 4, 5, 7, 6, 9, 8, 10, 11, 13, 12, 15, 14, 16, 17, 19, 18, 21, 20, 22]
  invFun := ![1, 0, 3, 2, 4, 5, 7, 6, 9, 8, 10, 11, 13, 12, 15, 14, 16, 17, 19, 18, 21, 20, 22]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- The generator `M23.b`, given by its tables of images and inverse images. -/
private def bTable : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![15, 8, 0, 4, 7, 21, 6, 22, 20, 9, 2, 1, 19, 17, 16, 10, 14, 5, 18, 12, 11, 13, 3]
  invFun := ![2, 11, 10, 22, 3, 17, 6, 4, 1, 9, 15, 20, 19, 21, 16, 0, 14, 13, 18, 12, 8, 5, 7]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

private theorem aTable_eq : aTable = a := by decide +kernel

private theorem bTable_eq : bTable = b := by decide +kernel

/-- The first ATLAS generator `a` has order `2`. -/
theorem orderOf_a : orderOf a = 2 :=
  orderOf_eq_prime (by decide +kernel) (by decide +kernel)

/-- The second ATLAS generator `b` has order `4`. -/
theorem orderOf_b : orderOf b = 4 :=
  orderOf_eq_prime_pow (p := 2) (n := 1) (by decide +kernel) (by decide +kernel)

/-- The product `a * b` of the ATLAS generators has order `23`. -/
theorem orderOf_a_mul_b : orderOf (a * b) = 23 :=
  have : Fact (Nat.Prime 23) := ⟨by decide⟩
  orderOf_eq_prime (by decide +kernel) (by decide +kernel)

/-! ### The presentation of `M₂₃` holds in the model -/

/-- The images in the permutation model of the generators of the presentation of `M₂₃`: `a` for
the generator of index `0` and `b⁻¹` for the generator of index `1`. -/
def presentationImage (i : Fin SporadicName.M23.presentation.generatorCount) :
    Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) :=
  if (i : ℕ) = 0 then a else b⁻¹

/-- The presentation generator of index `0` maps to `a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem presentationImage_zero (h : 0 < SporadicName.M23.presentation.generatorCount) :
    presentationImage ⟨0, h⟩ = a := by
  simp [presentationImage]

/-- The presentation generator of index `1` maps to `b⁻¹`. -/
@[simp]
theorem presentationImage_one (h : 1 < SporadicName.M23.presentation.generatorCount) :
    presentationImage ⟨1, h⟩ = b⁻¹ := by
  simp [presentationImage]

/-- The range of `presentationImage` is the pair `{a, b⁻¹}`. -/
theorem range_presentationImage : Set.range presentationImage = {a, b⁻¹} :=
  Set.range_ite_const ⟨⟨0, by simp⟩, rfl⟩ ⟨⟨1, by simp⟩, Nat.one_ne_zero⟩

/-- **The relators of `M₂₃` hold in the model.** All nine transcribed relators of the ATLAS
presentation `M23G1-P1` evaluate to `1` at `presentationImage`. -/
theorem lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one :
    ∀ t ∈ SporadicName.M23.presentation.transcribed,
      FreeGroup.lift presentationImage t.toFreeGroup = 1 := by
  -- The type of `presentationImage` mentions `SporadicName.M23.presentation`, so the statement is
  -- first abstracted over the presentation and then specialized along `presentation_M23`.
  suffices key : ∀ P : GroupPresentation, P = m23Presentation → ∀ t ∈ P.transcribed,
      FreeGroup.lift (fun i : Fin P.generatorCount ↦ if (i : ℕ) = 0 then aTable else bTable⁻¹)
        t.toFreeGroup = 1 by
    have himg : presentationImage =
        fun i : Fin SporadicName.M23.presentation.generatorCount ↦
          if (i : ℕ) = 0 then aTable else bTable⁻¹ := by
      ext i
      simp [presentationImage, aTable_eq, bTable_eq]
    rw [himg]
    exact key _ SporadicName.presentation_M23
  rintro P rfl
  simp only [m23Presentation_transcribed, List.mem_cons, List.not_mem_nil, or_false,
    forall_eq_or_imp, forall_eq, Relator.lift_toFreeGroup, Relator.eval_mul, Relator.eval_pow,
    Relator.eval_inv, Relator.eval_comm, Relator.eval_gen, one_ne_zero, ↓reduceIte]
  decide +kernel

/-- **The images generate the model.** The subgroup generated by the images `a` and `b⁻¹` of the
presentation generators is the permutation model `M23`. -/
theorem closure_range_presentationImage :
    Subgroup.closure (Set.range presentationImage) = M23 := by
  rw [range_presentationImage, M23_def, Set.insert_eq, Set.insert_eq, Subgroup.closure_union,
    Subgroup.closure_union, Subgroup.closure_singleton_inv]

/-- The homomorphism from the group presented by the presentation of `M₂₃` to
`Equiv.Perm (Fin 23)` sending the presentation generators to `presentationImage`. -/
def presentationHom : SporadicName.M23.Group →* Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) :=
  SporadicName.M23.presentation.homEquiv.symm
    ⟨presentationImage, lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one⟩

/-- `presentationHom` sends the `i`-th presentation generator to `presentationImage i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem presentationHom_of (i : Fin SporadicName.M23.presentation.generatorCount) :
    presentationHom (PresentedGroup.of i) = presentationImage i :=
  GroupPresentation.homEquiv_symm_apply_of _ _ i

/-- The range of `presentationHom` is the permutation model `M23`. -/
theorem range_presentationHom : presentationHom.range = M23 :=
  (GroupPresentation.range_homEquiv_symm _ _).trans closure_range_presentationImage

end M23

/-- **The presented group of `M₂₃` maps onto the permutation model.** The group defined by the
presentation of `M₂₃` carried by `TauCeti.SporadicName.presentation` has a surjective homomorphism
onto `M23`. -/
theorem exists_surjective_M23 :
    ∃ f : SporadicName.M23.Group →* M23, Function.Surjective f :=
  SporadicName.M23.presentation.exists_surjective_of_closure_range_eq
    ⟨M23.presentationImage, M23.lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one⟩
    M23.closure_range_presentationImage

/-- The permutation model `M23` is nontrivial: it contains the involution `M23.a`. -/
instance : Nontrivial M23 :=
  M23.nontrivial_iff_exists_ne_one.2 ⟨M23.a, M23.a_mem, by decide +kernel⟩

/-- The group presented by the presentation of `M₂₃` is nontrivial, since it maps onto the
nontrivial permutation model `M23`. -/
instance : Nontrivial SporadicName.M23.Group :=
  exists_surjective_M23.choose_spec.nontrivial

/-! ### The order of the model -/

namespace M23

/- The kernel evaluates a permutation given by its tables of images and inverse images much faster
than a product of cycles or a long word, so the sifting computations below run on `aTable`,
`bTable`, and thirteen further elements of `M23`, those of level `i` fixing `0, …, i - 1`. Each
table of level `i ≥ 1` is checked once to be a word in the tables of the preceding levels, and the
representatives along the base are products of at most three of these fifteen tables and their
inverses, so that sifting stays cheap. -/

/-- An involution of `M23` fixing `0`, given by its table of images; by `g1_eq` it is a word in
the ATLAS generators. -/
private def g1 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 4, 2, 3, 1, 5, 6, 22, 21, 14, 16, 12, 11, 19, 9, 15, 10, 18, 17, 13, 20, 8, 7]
  invFun := ![0, 4, 2, 3, 1, 5, 6, 22, 21, 14, 16, 12, 11, 19, 9, 15, 10, 18, 17, 13, 20, 8, 7]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- A permutation of `M23` fixing `0`, given by its tables of images and inverse images; by `h1_eq`
it is a word in the ATLAS generators. -/
private def h1 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 5, 1, 4, 7, 2, 10, 11, 18, 19, 6, 14, 21, 8, 15, 3, 22, 20, 13, 17, 16, 12, 9]
  invFun := ![0, 2, 5, 15, 3, 1, 10, 4, 13, 22, 6, 7, 21, 18, 11, 14, 20, 19, 8, 9, 17, 12, 16]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- An involution of `M23` fixing `0, 1, 2, 3, 4`, given by its table of images; by `g2_eq` it is
a word in the tables of level `1`. -/
private def g2 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 22, 5, 17, 11, 10, 9, 18, 20, 21, 19, 16, 8, 12, 15, 13, 14, 6]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 22, 5, 17, 11, 10, 9, 18, 20, 21, 19, 16, 8, 12, 15, 13, 14, 6]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- A permutation of `M23` fixing `0, 1`, given by its tables of images and inverse images; by
`h2_eq` it is a word in the tables of level `1`. -/
private def h2 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 11, 2, 19, 5, 9, 12, 16, 18, 6, 17, 13, 21, 4, 7, 14, 22, 20, 8, 10, 15, 3]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 3, 22, 14, 5, 10, 15, 19, 6, 20, 2, 7, 12, 16, 21, 8, 11, 9, 4, 18, 13, 17]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- A permutation of `M23` fixing `0, 1, 2`, given by its tables of images and inverse images; by
`g3_eq` it is a word in the tables of level `2`. -/
private def g3 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 2, 11, 19, 18, 22, 17, 5, 3, 14, 9, 7, 13, 21, 4, 6, 12, 8, 15, 20, 10, 16]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 2, 9, 15, 8, 16, 12, 18, 11, 21, 3, 17, 13, 10, 19, 22, 7, 5, 4, 20, 14, 6]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- A permutation of `M23` fixing `0, 1, 2`, given by its tables of images and inverse images; by
`h3_eq` it is a word in the tables of level `2`. -/
private def h3 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 2, 6, 11, 17, 8, 9, 7, 3, 14, 18, 21, 12, 5, 10, 19, 15, 20, 13, 22, 16, 4]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 2, 9, 22, 14, 3, 8, 6, 7, 15, 4, 13, 19, 10, 17, 21, 5, 11, 16, 18, 12, 20]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- A permutation of `M23` fixing `0, 1, 2, 3`, given by its tables of images and inverse images;
by `g4_eq` it is a word in the tables of level `3`. -/
private def g4 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 16, 21, 11, 5, 22, 17, 4, 19, 13, 15, 14, 12, 10, 18, 9, 6, 8, 7, 20]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 10, 7, 19, 21, 20, 18, 16, 6, 15, 12, 14, 13, 4, 9, 17, 11, 22, 5, 8]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- A permutation of `M23` fixing `0, 1, 2, 3`, given by its tables of images and inverse images;
by `h4_eq` it is a word in the tables of level `3`. -/
private def h4 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 16, 22, 19, 18, 21, 20, 4, 11, 8, 9, 6, 7, 10, 5, 15, 14, 13, 12, 17]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 10, 17, 14, 15, 12, 13, 16, 11, 21, 20, 19, 18, 4, 22, 7, 6, 9, 8, 5]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- A permutation of `M23` fixing `0, 1, 2, 3`, given by its tables of images and inverse images;
by `k4_eq` it is a word in the tables of level `3`. -/
private def k4 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 10, 22, 13, 12, 15, 14, 16, 5, 20, 21, 18, 19, 4, 17, 9, 8, 7, 6, 11]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 16, 11, 21, 20, 19, 18, 4, 22, 7, 6, 9, 8, 10, 17, 14, 15, 12, 13, 5]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- An involution of `M23` fixing `0, 1, 2, 3, 4`, given by its table of images; by `g5_eq` it is
a word in the tables of level `4`. -/
private def g5 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 18, 14, 12, 13, 15, 10, 19, 7, 8, 6, 9, 16, 20, 5, 11, 17, 22, 21]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 18, 14, 12, 13, 15, 10, 19, 7, 8, 6, 9, 16, 20, 5, 11, 17, 22, 21]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- An involution of `M23` fixing `0, 1, 2, 3, 4`, given by its table of images; by `h5_eq` it is
a word in the tables of level `4`. -/
private def h5 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 20, 15, 13, 12, 14, 10, 21, 8, 7, 9, 6, 16, 18, 17, 22, 5, 11, 19]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 20, 15, 13, 12, 14, 10, 21, 8, 7, 9, 6, 16, 18, 17, 22, 5, 11, 19]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- An involution of `M23` fixing `0, 1, 2, 3, 4`, given by its table of images; by `k5_eq` it is
a word in the tables of level `4`. -/
private def k5 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 5, 22, 11, 17, 10, 8, 21, 19, 18, 20, 16, 9, 14, 13, 15, 12, 7]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 5, 22, 11, 17, 10, 8, 21, 19, 18, 20, 16, 9, 14, 13, 15, 12, 7]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

/-- An involution of `M23` fixing `0, 1, 2, 3, 4`, given by its table of images; by `l5_eq` it is
a word in `g2`, `g5`, `h5` and `k5`. -/
private def l5 : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23) where
  toFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 11, 8, 9, 6, 7, 10, 5, 15, 14, 13, 12, 16, 22, 19, 18, 21, 20, 17]
  invFun := ![0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 11, 8, 9, 6, 7, 10, 5, 15, 14, 13, 12, 16, 22, 19, 18, 21, 20, 17]
  left_inv := by decide
  right_inv := by decide

private theorem g1_eq : g1 = aTable * bTable * aTable * bTable⁻¹ * aTable := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem h1_eq :
    h1 = bTable⁻¹ * aTable * bTable * aTable * bTable * aTable * bTable := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem g2_eq : g2 = h1 * g1 * h1⁻¹ := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem h2_eq : h2 = h1 * h1 * g1 * h1 := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem g3_eq : g3 = g2 * h2 * g2 * h2⁻¹ := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem h3_eq : h3 = g2 * h2 * h2 * g2 * h2 * g2 * h2⁻¹ * h2⁻¹ * g2 * h2 := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem g4_eq : g4 = g3 * h3⁻¹ := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem h4_eq : h4 = g3⁻¹ * h3 * h3 * g3 * h3 := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem k4_eq : k4 = g3⁻¹ * h3⁻¹ * g3⁻¹ * h3 * h3 := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem g5_eq : g5 = g4 * h4⁻¹ := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem h5_eq : h5 = g4 * k4 := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem k5_eq : k5 = g4⁻¹ * k4⁻¹ := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem l5_eq : l5 = g2 * g5 * h5 * k5 := by
  decide +kernel

/-- The fifteen tables lie in `M23`. -/
private theorem tables_mem :
    aTable ∈ M23 ∧ bTable ∈ M23 ∧ g1 ∈ M23 ∧ h1 ∈ M23 ∧ g2 ∈ M23 ∧ h2 ∈ M23 ∧ g3 ∈ M23 ∧
      h3 ∈ M23 ∧ g4 ∈ M23 ∧ h4 ∈ M23 ∧ k4 ∈ M23 ∧ g5 ∈ M23 ∧ h5 ∈ M23 ∧ k5 ∈ M23 ∧
      l5 ∈ M23 := by
  have ha : aTable ∈ M23 := aTable_eq ▸ a_mem
  have hb : bTable ∈ M23 := bTable_eq ▸ b_mem
  have hg1 : g1 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [g1_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right ha, mul_mem_cancel_right hb,
      mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hb), ha]
  have hh1 : h1 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [h1_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right ha, mul_mem_cancel_right hb, inv_mem_iff, hb]
  have hg2 : g2 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [g2_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right hg1, mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hh1), hh1]
  have hh2 : h2 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [h2_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right hg1, mul_mem_cancel_right hh1, hh1]
  have hg3 : g3 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [g3_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right hg2, mul_mem_cancel_right hh2,
      mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hh2), hg2]
  have hh3 : h3 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [h3_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right hg2, mul_mem_cancel_right hh2,
      mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hh2), hg2]
  have hg4 : g4 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [g4_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hh3), hg3]
  have hh4 : h4 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [h4_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right hg3, mul_mem_cancel_right hh3, inv_mem_iff, hg3]
  have hk4 : k4 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [k4_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hg3), mul_mem_cancel_right hh3,
      mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hh3), inv_mem_iff, hg3]
  have hg5 : g5 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [g5_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hh4), hg4]
  have hh5 : h5 ∈ M23 := h5_eq ▸ mul_mem hg4 hk4
  have hk5 : k5 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [k5_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hk4), inv_mem_iff, hg4]
  have hl5 : l5 ∈ M23 := by
    simp only [l5_eq, mul_mem_cancel_right hg5, mul_mem_cancel_right hh5,
      mul_mem_cancel_right hk5, hg2]
  exact ⟨ha, hb, hg1, hh1, hg2, hh2, hg3, hh3, hg4, hh4, hk4, hg5, hh5, hk5, hl5⟩

/-- Representatives along the base `0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5`: for `i < 6`, the list `transversal i`
consists of elements of `M23`, written as products of at most three of the tables above and their
inverses, that fix `0, …, i - 1` and send `i` to each point of its basic orbit, in increasing
order. -/
private def transversal : ℕ → List (Equiv.Perm (Fin 23))
  | 0 => [1, aTable, bTable⁻¹, aTable * bTable⁻¹, g1 * aTable, h1 * aTable, h5 * bTable,
      h2 * bTable, bTable * aTable, g5 * bTable, bTable * bTable, bTable⁻¹ * aTable, g4 * bTable,
      g4⁻¹ * bTable, aTable * bTable, bTable, bTable * aTable * bTable, h3⁻¹ * bTable,
      h4⁻¹ * bTable, g2 * bTable, k5 * bTable, h2⁻¹ * bTable, bTable * h2 * bTable]
  | 1 => [1, h1⁻¹, h1⁻¹ * g1, g1, h1, k5 * h1, h1 * g1, g3⁻¹ * h1, g1 * h2⁻¹ * g1, g4⁻¹ * g1,
      h2 * h1⁻¹, g1 * h2 * h1⁻¹, g1 * h2 * g1, h2⁻¹ * g1, g3⁻¹ * g1, g4 * g1, h3 * h1, g3 * h1,
      h2 * g1, h5 * h1, g4 * h1, h3⁻¹ * g1]
  | 2 => [1, h2⁻¹, h3⁻¹ * h2, k4 * h2, h3 * h2⁻¹, g2 * k4 * h2, k5 * h2, g2 * h2,
      h2⁻¹ * h3 * h2⁻¹, h2, g2 * h3 * h2, h2⁻¹ * h5 * h2, g2 * h5 * h2, g2 * g4 * h2,
      h2 * k5 * h2, h2 * h2, h3 * h2, g4 * h2, h2 * h3 * h2, h5 * h2, h2⁻¹ * h2⁻¹]
  | 3 => [1, h3⁻¹ * g3, k4 * g3, h3, h3⁻¹ * g3⁻¹, h3 * h3, g3⁻¹, g3 * k4⁻¹ * h3, g3,
      g2 * h3 * g3, h4⁻¹ * g3⁻¹, h4⁻¹ * h3, g5 * g3⁻¹, g3⁻¹ * h3, g4 * g3⁻¹, h3 * g3, g4 * g3,
      h4 * g3⁻¹, k4⁻¹ * h3, g2 * h3]
  | 4 => [1, g4⁻¹, g4]
  | 5 => [1, k5, g2, k5 * l5, g2 * l5, l5, g2 * g5, g2 * h5, g5 * k5, h5 * k5, g5 * h5, g5,
      g5 * l5, h5, h5 * l5, g2 * k5]
  | _ => []

private theorem mem_of_mem_transversal {i : ℕ} {r : Equiv.Perm (Fin 23)} (hr : r ∈ transversal i) :
    r ∈ M23 := by
  obtain ⟨ha, hb, hg1, hh1, hg2, hh2, hg3, hh3, hg4, hh4, hk4, hg5, hh5, hk5, hl5⟩ := tables_mem
  revert r
  match i with
  | 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 =>
    simp only [transversal, List.forall_mem_cons, List.not_mem_nil, IsEmpty.forall_iff,
      implies_true, and_true, mul_mem_cancel_right ha, mul_mem_cancel_right hb,
      mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hb), mul_mem_cancel_right hg1, mul_mem_cancel_right hh1,
      mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hh1), mul_mem_cancel_right hh2,
      mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hh2), mul_mem_cancel_right hg3,
      mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hg3), mul_mem_cancel_right hh3, mul_mem_cancel_right hg4,
      mul_mem_cancel_right hk4, mul_mem_cancel_right (inv_mem hk4), mul_mem_cancel_right hg5,
      mul_mem_cancel_right hh5, mul_mem_cancel_right hk5, mul_mem_cancel_right hl5, inv_mem_iff,
      ha, hb, hg1, hh1, hg2, hh2, hg3, hh3, hg4, hh4, hk4, hg5, hh5, hk5, hl5, one_mem]
  | _ + 6 => simp [transversal]

private theorem mem_transversal : ∀ i < 6, ∀ r ∈ transversal i, r ∈ M23 :=
  fun _ _ _ ↦ mem_of_mem_transversal

private theorem le_closure_tables : M23 ≤ Subgroup.closure {g | g ∈ [aTable, bTable]} := by
  rw [M23_def, aTable_eq, bTable_eq]
  exact Subgroup.closure_mono (by simp [Set.insert_subset_iff])

private theorem transversalCheck_eq_true :
    TauCeti.transversalCheck (Fin.ofNat 23) transversal 6 = true := by
  decide +kernel

private theorem sift_tables :
    [aTable, bTable].all (TauCeti.sift (Fin.ofNat 23) transversal 0 6 1) = true := by
  decide +kernel

/- Split the sifting checks by both levels `i` and `j`, so each kernel computation checks only
one pair of transversal lists and stays comfortably within the default heartbeat budget. -/
private def siftPairCheck (i j : ℕ) : Bool :=
  (transversal j).all fun s ↦ (transversal i).all fun r ↦
    TauCeti.sift (Fin.ofNat 23) transversal i (6 - i) 1 (s * r)

private theorem siftCheck_eq_all (i : ℕ) :
    TauCeti.siftCheck (Fin.ofNat 23) transversal 6 i =
      ((List.range 6).filter (i ≤ ·)).all (siftPairCheck i) :=
  rfl

private theorem siftPairCheck_0_0 : siftPairCheck 0 0 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_0_1 : siftPairCheck 0 1 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_0_2 : siftPairCheck 0 2 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_0_3 : siftPairCheck 0 3 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_0_4 : siftPairCheck 0 4 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_0_5 : siftPairCheck 0 5 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_1_1 : siftPairCheck 1 1 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_1_2 : siftPairCheck 1 2 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_1_3 : siftPairCheck 1 3 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_1_4 : siftPairCheck 1 4 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_1_5 : siftPairCheck 1 5 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_2_2 : siftPairCheck 2 2 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_2_3 : siftPairCheck 2 3 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_2_4 : siftPairCheck 2 4 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_2_5 : siftPairCheck 2 5 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_3_3 : siftPairCheck 3 3 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_3_4 : siftPairCheck 3 4 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_3_5 : siftPairCheck 3 5 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_4_4 : siftPairCheck 4 4 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_4_5 : siftPairCheck 4 5 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftPairCheck_5_5 : siftPairCheck 5 5 = true := by decide +kernel

private theorem siftCheck_eq_true :
    ∀ i < 6, TauCeti.siftCheck (Fin.ofNat 23) transversal 6 i = true := by
  intro i hi
  rw [siftCheck_eq_all]
  interval_cases i
  · have hr : (List.range 6).filter (0 ≤ ·) = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5] := by decide
    simp only [hr, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, siftPairCheck_0_0, siftPairCheck_0_1,
      siftPairCheck_0_2, siftPairCheck_0_3, siftPairCheck_0_4, siftPairCheck_0_5, Bool.true_and]
  · have hr : (List.range 6).filter (1 ≤ ·) = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] := by decide
    simp only [hr, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, siftPairCheck_1_1, siftPairCheck_1_2,
      siftPairCheck_1_3, siftPairCheck_1_4, siftPairCheck_1_5, Bool.true_and]
  · have hr : (List.range 6).filter (2 ≤ ·) = [2, 3, 4, 5] := by decide
    simp only [hr, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, siftPairCheck_2_2, siftPairCheck_2_3,
      siftPairCheck_2_4, siftPairCheck_2_5, Bool.true_and]
  · have hr : (List.range 6).filter (3 ≤ ·) = [3, 4, 5] := by decide
    simp only [hr, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, siftPairCheck_3_3, siftPairCheck_3_4,
      siftPairCheck_3_5, Bool.true_and]
  · have hr : (List.range 6).filter (4 ≤ ·) = [4, 5] := by decide
    simp only [hr, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, siftPairCheck_4_4, siftPairCheck_4_5, Bool.true_and]
  · have hr : (List.range 6).filter (5 ≤ ·) = [5] := by decide
    simp only [hr, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, siftPairCheck_5_5, Bool.true_and]

/-- **The points `0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5` form a base of `M23`**: no element of `M23` other than `1`
fixes all of them. -/
theorem stabilizerChain_six_eq_bot : M23.stabilizerChain (Fin.ofNat 23) 6 = ⊥ :=
  Subgroup.stabilizerChain_eq_bot_of_siftCheck le_closure_tables
    transversalCheck_eq_true sift_tables siftCheck_eq_true

/-- **The model `M23` acts `4`-transitively on its `23` points.** Every injective `4`-tuple in
`Fin 23` lies in the `M23`-orbit of `(0, 1, 2, 3)` by successive multiplication from the first four
transversal lists. -/
instance isMultiplyPretransitive_four : MulAction.IsMultiplyPretransitive M23 (Fin 23) 4 := by
  have h0 : ∀ y : Fin 23, ∃ r ∈ transversal 0, r 0 = y := by decide +kernel
  have h1 : ∀ y : Fin 23, y ≠ 0 → ∃ r ∈ transversal 1, r 0 = 0 ∧ r 1 = y := by decide +kernel
  have h2 : ∀ y : Fin 23, y ≠ 0 → y ≠ 1 →
      ∃ r ∈ transversal 2, r 0 = 0 ∧ r 1 = 1 ∧ r 2 = y := by decide +kernel
  have h3 : ∀ y : Fin 23, y ≠ 0 → y ≠ 1 → y ≠ 2 →
      ∃ r ∈ transversal 3, r 0 = 0 ∧ r 1 = 1 ∧ r 2 = 2 ∧ r 3 = y := by decide +kernel
  refine MulAction.IsPretransitive.of_orbit (x₀ := Fin.castLEEmb (by decide)) fun x ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨r0, hr0, hx0⟩ := h0 (x 0)
  have hy1_0 : r0⁻¹ (x 1) ≠ 0 := by
    intro heq
    exact x.injective.ne (by decide : (1 : Fin 4) ≠ 0)
      (by simpa [hx0] using congrArg r0 heq)
  obtain ⟨r1, hr1, hr1_0, hx1⟩ := h1 (r0⁻¹ (x 1)) hy1_0
  have hg1_0 : (r0 * r1) 0 = x 0 := by simp [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hr1_0, hx0]
  have hg1_1 : (r0 * r1) 1 = x 1 := by simp [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hx1]
  have hy2_0 : (r0 * r1)⁻¹ (x 2) ≠ 0 := by
    intro heq
    exact x.injective.ne (by decide : (2 : Fin 4) ≠ 0)
      (by simpa [hg1_0] using congrArg (r0 * r1) heq)
  have hy2_1 : (r0 * r1)⁻¹ (x 2) ≠ 1 := by
    intro heq
    exact x.injective.ne (by decide : (2 : Fin 4) ≠ 1)
      (by simpa [hg1_1] using congrArg (r0 * r1) heq)
  obtain ⟨r2, hr2, hr2_0, hr2_1, hx2⟩ := h2 ((r0 * r1)⁻¹ (x 2)) hy2_0 hy2_1
  have hg2_0 : (r0 * r1 * r2) 0 = x 0 := by simp [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hr2_0, hg1_0]
  have hg2_1 : (r0 * r1 * r2) 1 = x 1 := by simp [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hr2_1, hg1_1]
  have hg2_2 : (r0 * r1 * r2) 2 = x 2 := by
    simpa [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply] using congrArg (r0 * r1) hx2
  have hy3_0 : (r0 * r1 * r2)⁻¹ (x 3) ≠ 0 := by
    intro heq
    exact x.injective.ne (by decide : (3 : Fin 4) ≠ 0)
      (by simpa [hg2_0] using congrArg (r0 * r1 * r2) heq)
  have hy3_1 : (r0 * r1 * r2)⁻¹ (x 3) ≠ 1 := by
    intro heq
    exact x.injective.ne (by decide : (3 : Fin 4) ≠ 1)
      (by simpa [hg2_1] using congrArg (r0 * r1 * r2) heq)
  have hy3_2 : (r0 * r1 * r2)⁻¹ (x 3) ≠ 2 := by
    intro heq
    exact x.injective.ne (by decide : (3 : Fin 4) ≠ 2)
      (by simpa [hg2_2] using congrArg (r0 * r1 * r2) heq)
  obtain ⟨r3, hr3, hr3_0, hr3_1, hr3_2, hx3⟩ := h3 ((r0 * r1 * r2)⁻¹ (x 3)) hy3_0 hy3_1 hy3_2
  refine ⟨⟨r0 * r1 * r2 * r3, mul_mem (mul_mem (mul_mem (mem_of_mem_transversal hr0)
      (mem_of_mem_transversal hr1)) (mem_of_mem_transversal hr2))
      (mem_of_mem_transversal hr3)⟩, ?_⟩
  rw [Subgroup.mk_smul]
  apply DFunLike.ext
  rintro ⟨j, hj⟩
  rw [FunLike.coe_smul, Pi.smul_apply, Equiv.Perm.smul_def]
  match j with
  | 0 =>
    have hcast : (Fin.castLEEmb (by decide : 4 ≤ 23)) ⟨0, hj⟩ = 0 := rfl
    have hx : x ⟨0, hj⟩ = x 0 := rfl
    rw [hcast, hx, Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hr3_0]
    exact hg2_0
  | 1 =>
    have hcast : (Fin.castLEEmb (by decide : 4 ≤ 23)) ⟨1, hj⟩ = 1 := rfl
    have hx : x ⟨1, hj⟩ = x 1 := rfl
    rw [hcast, hx, Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hr3_1]
    exact hg2_1
  | 2 =>
    have hcast : (Fin.castLEEmb (by decide : 4 ≤ 23)) ⟨2, hj⟩ = 2 := rfl
    have hx : x ⟨2, hj⟩ = x 2 := rfl
    rw [hcast, hx, Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hr3_2]
    exact hg2_2
  | 3 =>
    have hcast : (Fin.castLEEmb (by decide : 4 ≤ 23)) ⟨3, hj⟩ = 3 := rfl
    have hx : x ⟨3, hj⟩ = x 3 := rfl
    rw [hcast, hx, Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hx3]
    simp
  | n + 4 => omega

/-- The model acts `3`-transitively on its `23` points. -/
instance isMultiplyPretransitive_three : MulAction.IsMultiplyPretransitive M23 (Fin 23) 3 :=
  MulAction.isMultiplyPretransitive_of_le (n := 4) (by decide) (by simp)

/-- The model acts doubly transitively on its `23` points. -/
instance isMultiplyPretransitive_two : MulAction.IsMultiplyPretransitive M23 (Fin 23) 2 :=
  MulAction.isMultiplyPretransitive_of_le (n := 4) (by decide) (by simp)

/-- The model acts transitively on its `23` points. -/
instance isPretransitive : MulAction.IsPretransitive M23 (Fin 23) :=
  MulAction.isPretransitive_of_is_two_pretransitive

/-- The model acts primitively on its `23` points. -/
instance isPreprimitive : MulAction.IsPreprimitive M23 (Fin 23) :=
  MulAction.isPreprimitive_of_is_two_pretransitive isMultiplyPretransitive_two

end M23

/-- **The order of `M₂₃`.** The permutation model `M23` has
`10200960 = 23 * 22 * 21 * 20 * 3 * 16` elements: along the base `0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5` its basic
orbits have lengths `23`, `22`, `21`, `20`, `3` and `16`. -/
theorem card_M23 : Nat.card M23 = 10200960 := by
  rw [Subgroup.natCard_eq_prod_length_of_siftCheck M23.mem_transversal M23.le_closure_tables
    M23.transversalCheck_eq_true M23.sift_tables M23.siftCheck_eq_true]
  decide

/-- The group presented by the presentation of `M₂₃`, when finite, has at least `10200960`
elements, since it maps onto the model `M23`. Finiteness is a hypothesis: with the junk value
`Nat.card = 0` for infinite types, a surjection alone gives no lower bound. -/
theorem le_natCard_group_M23 (h : 0 < Nat.card SporadicName.M23.Group) :
    10200960 ≤ Nat.card SporadicName.M23.Group := by
  have := Nat.finite_of_card_ne_zero h.ne'
  obtain ⟨f, hf⟩ := exists_surjective_M23
  exact card_M23 ▸ Nat.card_le_card_of_surjective f hf

end TauCeti.Sporadic
